@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Login as customer1 (owns order-1 and order-2)
# @name cust1Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer1@addiseats.et",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### 2. Login as customer2 (owns order-3; stranger to order-1)
# @name cust2Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer2@addiseats.et",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### 3. Login as courier (assigned to order-1 and order-2)
# @name courierLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "courier@addiseats.et",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### 4. Login as staff (bypass policy & sees all orders)
# @name staffLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "staff@addiseats.et",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### 5. Collection scoping: customer1 sees only their 2 orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cust1Login.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 6. Collection scoping: customer2 sees only their 1 order
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cust2Login.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 7. Collection scoping: courier sees only assigned orders (2 orders)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{courierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 8. Collection scoping: staff sees all seeded orders (3 orders)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{staffLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 9. Stranger order -> 404 Not Found (customer2 requesting order-1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/order-1
Authorization: Bearer {{cust2Login.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 10. Forbidden role/action on accessible order -> 403 Forbidden (customer1 trying to updateStatus on order-1)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/orders/order-1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{cust1Login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "delivered"
}

###

### 11. Allowed cancel by owner on pending order -> 200 OK (customer1 cancelling order-1)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/orders/order-1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{cust1Login.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 12. Staff bypass -> 200 OK (staff updating status on order-3)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/orders/order-3/status
Authorization: Bearer {{staffLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "preparing"
}

### 13. Register a new user -> 201 Created (returns SafeUser without passwordHash/refreshHash)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@addiseats.et",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### 14. Duplicate registration -> 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@addiseats.et",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### 15. Check current authenticated user -> 200 OK (shows id, email, roles, restaurantId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{staffLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 16. Refresh tokens -> 200 OK (rotates accessToken and refreshToken)
# @name rotatedTokens
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{cust1Login.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 17. Reuse old rotated refresh token -> 401 Unauthorized (invalidates stored refreshHash)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{cust1Login.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}